AUTHOR     (R.PRASAD, D.C.SARKAR)                                 30007  1    6 
TITLE      Measurement of (n,p) and (n,a) reaction cross sections 30007  1    7 
           at 14.8 MeV.                                           30007  1    8 
FACILITY   (CCW) 130 keV Cockcroft-Walton accelerator.            30007  1    9 
INC-SOURCE (D-T) Deuteron-tritium.                                30007  1   10 
SAMPLE     Powdery samples were uniformly spread in a thin        30007  1   11 
            perspex ring and sandwiched between two cellulose     30007  1   12 
            tapes. Spectroscopically pure substances of chemical  30007  1   13 
            purity more than 99.9 percent were used.              30007  1   14 
METHOD     (ACTIV) Activation technique.                          30007  1   15 
DETECTOR   End-window beta-counter of 2.5 mg/sqcm window          30007  1   16 
            thickness.                                            30007  1   17 
           (SCIN)  ZnS-Lucite crystal mounted on a PM tube was    30007  1   18 
            used as flux monitor.                                 30007  1   19 
PART-DET   (B-) Decay beta-.                                      30007  1   20 
MONITOR    (26-FE-56(N,P)25-MN-56,,SIG)                           30007  1   21 
            Iron-26 n-p sigma value used was 126.mb               30007  1   22 
            at 14.8 MeV.                                          30007  1   23 
ERR-ANALYS The quoted error includes statistical errors,and other 30007  1   24 
           errors which may occur in estimation of total number of30007  1   25 
           nuclei in target material and in determination of      30007  1   26 
           effective flux. While statistical errors vary from case30007  1   27 
           to case, all other errors were estimated to be less    30007  1   28 
           than 3.percent.                                        30007  1   29 
COMMENT    Cross-reference=  the (n,p) cross sections have been   30007  1   30 
